{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"access","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Access","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6AccessV","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Access"},{"text":"? { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A schedule runs a system alongside the systems whose accesses don’t conflict with its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own. A system whose access is "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the default, runs alone."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Build an access by chaining what the system reads and writes:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".reads(Velocity.self).writes(Position.self)"},{"type":"text","text":". A system with an access must reach only the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"types it lists (a relation through its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Targets"},{"type":"text","text":", the hierarchy through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Targets<ChildOf>"},{"type":"text","text":"), and must not spawn or despawn entities directly; it can queue those"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changes as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Important","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In debug builds, a system that reaches a component or resource type its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type"